  {
    "sha": "9221ccc65d345db35a8bb1061fb058b3748a6969",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDkyMjFjY2M2NWQzNDVkYjM1YThiYjEwNjFmYjA1OGIzNzQ4YTY5Njk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T09:42:58Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T09:42:58Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): refuse a tool file whose length unit no unit context states\n\nThe Part 21 parser maps short names such as A2PL3D and LNGUNT, but not\nthe short forms of GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT and SI_UNIT. A short-name\ntool file thus gave a CIP but no unit context, and the reader placed it\nat 1 mm per unit: an inch or metre file 25.4 or 1000 times too small.\n\nmm_per_unit now refuses by name when no context states a length unit but\nthe file has one (LENGTH_UNIT, an SI_UNIT of the metre, or a\nCONVERSION_BASED_UNIT over a LENGTH_MEASURE_WITH_UNIT). A file with no\nunit record keeps 1 mm per unit, as the ruststep reader did.\n\nAlso fixes two stale comments (review of PR #2918).\n\nRefs #2789\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
